{"availability":"available","full":"simbonk/holodeck","name":"holodeck","description":"Holodeck by chat","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-03T03:43:05Z","updated":"2026-10-08T06:39:13Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://holodeck-two.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://holodeck-two.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T06:39:25.342Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T06:39:25.342Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T06:39:25.342Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T06:39:25.342Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A single-file, AI-run text adventure powered by Google Gemini. Say how much time you have and the feeling you want, pick a curated story or a plot-free experience (or just upload a photo), and a Game Master builds a world just for you, keeps an eye on the clock, lands a real ending, and grades the result with a report card. Play by typing or hands-free by voice."],"features":["Play by the clock, not by turns: choose 10 minutes to 2 hours. The app learns your pace, estimates how many replies are left, starts wrapping up about three replies from the end, and lands a storybook ending in time.…","The feeling comes first: describe the feeling you want to come away with in your own words (or press Suggest some feelings, which builds on anything you have typed). It goes into the bible and is the Game Master's main…","It notices when you're happy: every turn the memory pass also reads your mood. When the feeling is landing or you are clearly enjoying a character or place, the plot steps aside: no interruptions, no new complications,…","Two ways to play: a curated story (a hidden roadmap timed to the session, which bends or waits for you) or an experience simulator (no plot points at all: a richly painted world, your own goal, and the feeling).","Personal details: your name, gender and who you're interested in (both free tex